{"id":"bang-patrol-4","title":"BANG, REDFISH and SHAD against convoy TAKA-206","short":"Patrol 4 · TAKA-206","eyebrow":"East of Formosa · Coordinated attack group \"Sandy's Sluggers\", Cdr L. D. McGregor in REDFISH","lede":"The three boats' torpedo attacks of 22–23 November 1944, as typed on their attack sheets, beside the log the convoy's minesweeper W-15 kept of the same night. Times are converted to GMT, so BANG and SHAD (zone K) and the Japanese escorts (zone I) share one clock.","places":[{"name":"Formosa","lon":121.35,"lat":24.0,"inset":[120.4,22.6]},{"name":"Yonaguni","lon":123.0,"lat":24.38,"small":true},{"name":"Iriomote","lon":123.82,"lat":24.2,"small":true},{"name":"Ishigaki","lon":124.17,"lat":24.3,"small":true}],"notes":[{"head":"Reading the map.","text":"Positions are each navigator's own dead reckoning; lines between them are straight. REDFISH's chronology position for Hozan Maru (24-27N 122-47E) is her own Attack 3 position, not the target's."},{"head":"Clocks.","text":"BANG, REDFISH and SHAD all kept zone K (−10) that night (the pack agreed \"all times ... will be minus ten (King)\"). Japanese records use Tokyo time (I, −9): Manazuru's red flare at 2240 I is 2340 K, 52 minutes before BANG's Attack 1."},{"head":"Who sank Hozan Maru.","text":"REDFISH heard \"first of many explosions; BANG apparently made her attack\" at 0037 K and fired her own first torpedoes at 0104 K. W-15 saw Hozan Maru torpedoed at 2339 I (0039 K). By the reports' own clocks the hit fits BANG's attack, not REDFISH's; the US credit to REDFISH appears to rest on her Attack 1 or 3 claim."},{"head":"Sources.","text":"War patrol reports, NARA microfilm M1752: BANG Patrol 4 (74802868), REDFISH Patrol 2 (74837267, 74837338), SHAD Patrol 8 (74848165). Minesweeper W-15's battle report on TAKA-206 via JACAR (C08030607900, National Institute for Defense Studies). Which ships sank, from combinedfleet.com, a secondary source, flagged where used. Coastline: Natural Earth."}],"boats":[{"id":"bang","name":"BANG","hull":"SS-385","co":"LCdr A. R. Gallaher","patrol_no":4},{"id":"redfish","name":"REDFISH","hull":"SS-395","co":"Cdr L. D. McGregor, pack commander","patrol_no":2},{"id":"shad","name":"SHAD","hull":"SS-235","co":"L. Julihn (middle initial illegible on the report)","patrol_no":8}],"others":[],"actions":[{"id":"taka-206","label":"22–23 November 1944","convoy":"TAKA-206","start":"1944-11-22T10:00Z","end":"1944-11-23T00:00Z","route":"Keelung → Naha, sailed 22 November.","ships_note":"Ships and escorts from W-15's battle report (JACAR C08030607900, p33).","outcome":"Three of the six ships were sunk (Hozan, Amakusa and Sakae Maru); Taiken, Sannin and Eikai Maru sheltered at Funauki (W-15's signal log). BANG claimed four sunk and one damaged; REDFISH two sunk (her Attacks 1 and 3, 0104 and 0141 K); SHAD's one salvo, fired by mistake at a torpedo boat at 2338 K, missed. The postwar credit gives BANG Sakae and Amakusa Maru and REDFISH Hozan Maru, but W-15 logged Hozan Maru torpedoed at 2339 I (0039 K), 25 minutes before REDFISH first fired and seven minutes after BANG's Attack 1.","ships":[{"name":"Taiken Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":false},{"name":"Hozan Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":true},{"name":"Sannin Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":false},{"name":"Amakusa Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":true},{"name":"Eikai Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":false},{"name":"Sakae Maru","kind":"Merchant","type":"cargo","sunk":true}],"escorts":[{"name":"Manazuru","kind":"Torpedo boat","type":"escort","sunk":false},{"name":"Seki Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false},{"name":"No. 16 Shonan Maru","kind":"Auxiliary escort","type":"gunboat","sunk":false},{"name":"W-15","kind":"Minesweeper","type":"escort","sunk":false}],"sil_note":"Silhouettes show the kind of ship (fleet submarine, destroyer, escort, auxiliary gunboat, merchant ship, tanker, fighter aircraft), not each one's own outline, and are not to scale.","box":[121.925,23.867,123.537,24.8],"tracks":{"bang":[{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-11-21T10:15Z","lat":24.3667,"lon":122.1167,"kind":"radar","ref":"Radar Nov 21b","on_track":true,"local":"1944-11-21 2015 (K)","raw":"24-22N 122-07E","note":"Radar intercept 167 MC","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802868/p32","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0113.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-11-22T14:32Z","lat":24.3917,"lon":122.6833,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 1","on_track":true,"local":"1944-11-23 0032 (K)","raw":"24-23.5N 122-41E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 1 (times not zoned; King per narrative)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802868/p12","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0093.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-11-22T14:33Z","lat":24.3917,"lon":122.6833,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 2","on_track":true,"local":"1944-11-23 0033 (K)","raw":"24-23.5N 122-41E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 2 (time 0032-50)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802868/p14","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0095.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-11-22T14:35Z","lat":24.3917,"lon":122.6833,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 3","on_track":true,"local":"1944-11-23 0035 (K)","raw":"24-23.5N 122-41E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 3 (time 0034-50)","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802868/p16","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-US_SubWarPatrolReports_1941-194/M1752_00051-00075/images/0097.jpg"},{"boat":"bang","utc":"1944-11-22T15:47Z","lat":24.4,"lon":122.75,"kind":"attack","ref":"Attack 4","on_track":true,"local":"1944-11-23 0147 (K)","raw":"24-24N 122-45E","note":"Torpedo attack No. 4","fix":"","page":"rg367-74802868/p18","scan":"https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/microfilm-publications/M1752-U